Files under prompts/ are verbatim copies kept as the reference for the /research-ta
agent definitions. They are NOT imported or executed by this project.

How this project adapts them (modifications are in separate files, not in these copies):
- .claude/agents/ta-*.md: role prompts rewritten in Korean for Korean equities research
  reports (not trading memos). Kept from the original: pre-fetched data instead of free
  tool calls for evidence, "say so explicitly if data is missing", debate opening rule
  (opponent_argument_or_opening), Hold-when-balanced rule, structured output fields of
  ResearchPlan / PortfolioDecision / SentimentReport.
- Removed: Trader entry/stop-loss/position sizing, US data vendors, LangGraph runtime.
- Changed: analysts run in parallel as Claude Code subagents; the number of analyst calls
  is decided by input data size (scripts/ta_plan_agents.py), not fixed at four.
- scripts/ta_market_data.py re-implements the 13 stockstats indicators used by the
  original market analyst and the stale-data guard/verified snapshot idea from
  dataflows/market_data_validator.py and stockstats_utils.py, without copying code.
